  "details": "At the top of [Terms of Service](https://hello.vrchat.com/legal) (dated August 15, 2025), there is a list of links, which \"you may be subject to the following terms and policies, which are incorporated by reference:\"\n\n- [Brand Guidelines](https://vrch.at/brand-guidelines)\n\n- [Community Guidelines](https://hello.vrchat.com/community-guidelines)\n\n- [Creator Economy Program Rules](https://hello.vrchat.com/legal/economy)\n\n- [Privacy Policy](https://hello.vrchat.com/privacy)\n\n- [SDK License](https://hello.vrchat.com/legal/sdk)\n\nAdditionally, on the footer of the VRChat.com website, there's another link: [Video Content Guidelines](https://hello.vrchat.com/video-content-guidelines), dated July 5, 2021. These video content guidelines also refer back to VRChat's Terms of Service in its text, and seem to be relevant to this preamble in Terms of Service, but a link to these Video Content Guidelines seems to be currently absent from the former list of links, while being prominently displayed in the footer of the website.",
